# vLLM flags for every fmtcmp LOGPROB CAPTURE (BF16 on the H100s, NVFP4 on Sparky).  One authority: both
# sparky_vllm_job.sh and h100/run_reference.sh read this file, so the two sides differ only in the weights,
# the platform (TP4 Hopper vs one GB10) and --gpu-memory-utilization.
# Deliberately NOT the cards' serving flags: no speculation (the capture is teacher-forced prefill), no prefix
# caching (a cached prefix has no prompt logprobs), and the Mamba state dtype left at the checkpoint's own
# default (config mamba_ssm_cache_dtype) on both sides instead of the Spark card's fp16 + stochastic rounding,
# so the comparison isolates the checkpoint.  Lines starting with # are comments; one flag (with value) a line.
--served-model-name fmtcmp
--trust-remote-code
--max-num-seqs 1
--max-num-batched-tokens 8192
--max-model-len 40960
--max-logprobs 64
--no-enable-prefix-caching
--seed 0
